      "id": 1,
      "text": "Kernville was founded in 1860 as Whiskey Flat, renamed in 1864 after whiskey dealer Adam Hamilton moved his shop from Quartzburg.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        9
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kernville%2C_California",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The town’s original site is now a California Historical Landmark #132, marking its early gold‑rush roots.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        2
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kernville%2C_California",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Kernville relocated upstream in 1951 to sit beside the tip of the northeast fork of Lake Isabella, preserving historic buildings.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        13
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kernville%2C_California",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "In 2004, local Rebecca Giddens earned a silver medal in Olympic K‑1 kayaking, training on Kern River’s white‑water course.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        1
      ],
